{
 "_doc": "Stream E (play-test 1, P19). Who walks the roads and who works the wilds — data for stream A to run. `kinds` = travelling groups that walk stream E's routes (data/provinces/torbor_downs-routes.json: town to town along B's roads). Each group is a crew of NPCs (`role` = a role id; its bark pool is chatter.json `role.<role>`), optionally with a pack animal or cart (a look only). `fights`: never = runs from danger (walks on, faster), defend = fights back only when hit, hunts = attacks monsters within 25 m of the road and helps players fighting near it. Display names: `{first}` = a given name from data/names/torbor.json `given` (f or m, seeded per traveller), `{family}` = a family name from the same file. `folk` = people who work one spot in the wilds: the placer (tools/place-vignettes.mjs) puts a `folk` placement {role, path} where `places`/`biomes`/`archetypes` fit; they walk a small loop of `loopM` metres, play the `work` animation at each stop, and bark from `chatter`. Pools: data/names/chatter.json. Speeds in metres a second (a player walks ~5).",
 "rules": {
  "perRouteKm": 0.6,
  "maxPerZone": 10,
  "minSpacingM": 120,
  "speedMps": 1.4,
  "waitAtTownMinutes": [
   2,
   6
  ],
  "night": "Fewer travellers at night: x0.4 of the day count, from kinds with night: true only. Patrols and couriers keep going.",
  "despawn": "A group despawns at its destination town gate; after waitAtTownMinutes a group of a fitting kind spawns at a random route end. Nobody spawns or despawns within 80 m of a player.",
  "fight": "never: walks on at x1.5 speed past a fight, cowers if cornered. defend: fights back only when hit, never chases more than 15 m off the road. hunts: attacks hostile monsters within 25 m of its route and joins any fight a player has within 25 m of it; it never leaves the road by more than 40 m. No traveller is attackable by players; monsters may attack anyone (a traveller that falls gets up after 60 s, nobody dies on the road for good).",
  "pairs": "Two of a crew walking within 4 m may trade a line and a reply (chatter.json `reply`) when a player is within 12 m, at most once a minute per group.",
  "stop": "A group pauses 5-20 s at a wayside, curio or crossing it passes (look about, sit, drink) — makes the road feel walked, not conveyed."
 },
